Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [sdist and wheel ship no LICENSE file despite declaring `license = "MIT"` in Cargo.toml/pyproject.toml/PyPI metadata; add the standard MIT text]

Neither the published sdist nor any of the six platform wheels contains a LICENSE
file: `[tool.maturin] exclude = ["LICENSE*"]` in pyproject.toml strips any LICENSE*
file from the wheel outright, and no LICENSE file is present in the sdist tree to
begin with. All three of Cargo.toml's `workspace.package.license`, pyproject.toml's
`project.license` and the PyPI "License" classifier say "MIT", and
`workspace.package.authors` names "Keeper Security Engineering
<pam@keepersecurity.com>", so add the standard MIT licence text under that
copyright and stop excluding it from the wheel, so the riscv64 wheel we publish
carries the licence its own metadata claims.

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -25,7 +25,6 @@

 [tool.maturin]
 module-name = "keeper_pam_webrtc_rs"
-exclude = ["LICENSE*"]
 manifest-path = "crates/webrtc-bindings/Cargo.toml"

 [tool.pytest.ini_options]
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
